# Admin — production build settings.
#
# Vite loads this automatically for `npm run build` and inlines the values at
# build time. Everything in a VITE_* variable ships inside the JavaScript
# bundle and is readable by anyone who opens the admin, so nothing secret goes
# here — the admin passcode is typed in at the gate and held in memory, and it
# must stay that way.

# Where the REST API lives. The /api suffix is part of it: the client asks for
# paths like /admin/summary, and this is what they hang off.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.skvpyros.in/api

# Two things the API has to be told before this works, both on its side:
#
#   Storefront:AllowedOrigins   must list this admin's own URL, or the browser
#                               blocks every response before the app sees it.
#   Storefront:Admin:Passcode   must be set, or every admin endpoint answers
#                               503 and the gate cannot let anyone in.
#
# See api/DEPLOYMENT.md.

# Where the "Open shop" link goes. Without it the link falls back to the
# storefront's dev server on localhost.
VITE_STOREFRONT_URL=https://skvpyros.in
